    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d481">

                <pb facs="0624" n="514" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg514"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/2808: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Shaw</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-21T16:00:00+00:00">November 21, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 21—11:20 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>774. From Ambassador Dawes: Sze confidentially informs me that at this
                    afternoon’s Council meeting he will propose a neutral and <pb facs="0625"
                        n="515" xml:id="pg515"/> nonpartisan commission. He has attempted to frame
                    this proposition so as to cause no immediate break.</p>
                <p>Referring to my 773, November 21, 3 p.m.,<anchor n="66" xml:id="d481-f1"/> giving
                    Sweetser’s report of the meeting yesterday, I have not made any commitments
                    concerning American membership on any body to be appointed and have said that
                    the United States would make a decision in this connection when the occasion so
                    required. [Dawes.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Shaw</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
